{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('paper_data.json'));f=p['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']\nprint('evidence meta', {k:v for k,v in f.items() if k\"'!='\"'episodes'})\nfor e in f['episodes']:\n print('EPISODE keys',list(e))\n print('meta',{k:v for k,v in e.items() if k\"'!='\"'solution'})\n print('solution keys',list(e['solution']))\n for c in e['solution']['cases']:\n  print('case',c['family'],c['case'],'n',len(c['observations']),'fail',c['failure'])\n print('first observation',json.dumps(e['solution']['cases'][0]['observations'][0]));break\nc=json.load(open('claims_grounding.json'))\nprint('grounding keys',list(c))\nfor i,v in enumerate(c['claims']):\n if i<5 or i>=101:print(i,v['claim'],'SOURCES',v.get('source_ids'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('paper_data.json'));f=p['final_evaluation']['evaluation_evidence']\nprint('evidence meta', {k:v for k,v in f.items() if k\"'!='\"'episodes'})\nfor e in f['episodes']:\n print('EPISODE keys',list(e))\n print('meta',{k:v for k,v in e.items() if k\"'!='\"'solution'})\n print('solution keys',list(e['solution']))\n for c in e['solution']['cases']:\n  print('case',c['family'],c['case'],'n',len(c['observations']),'fail',c['failure'])\n print('first observation',json.dumps(e['solution']['cases'][0]['observations'][0]));break\nc=json.load(open('claims_grounding.json'))\nprint('grounding keys',list(c))\nfor i,v in enumerate(c['claims']):\n if i<5 or i>=101:print(i,v['claim'],'SOURCES',v.get('source_ids'))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"evidence meta {'candidate_diagnostics_trust': 'unverified', 'episode_count': 3, 'path': 'work/results/a01/codex/20261107_023211/final_evaluation/results/evaluation_evidence.json', 'sha256': 'sha256:920cf164c9d4d64d7d52e141913d7ce3b910c04c74da9b960c178e37b33161a1', 'status': 'available'}\nEPISODE keys ['correct', 'duration_seconds', 'score', 'seed', 'solution']\nmeta {'correct': True, 'duration_seconds': 14.207079500891268, 'score': 0.6633040935672515, 'seed': 42011}\nsolution keys ['cases', 'replay', 'workers']\ncase helm original n 48 fail None\ncase helm permutation n 48 fail None\ncase helm constant n 48 fail None\ncase helm copy n 48 fail None\ncase openllm original n 48 fail None\ncase openllm permutation n 48 fail None\ncase openllm constant n 48 fail None\ncase openllm copy n 48 fail None\nfirst observation {\"allocation\": {\"status\": \"feasible\", \"tasks\": [55]}, \"baselines\": {\"greedy\": {\"attainable\": true, \"exact\": false, \"lower\": 0, \"tasks\": [55], \"upper\": 1}, \"none\": {\"attainable\": true, \"exact\": false, \"lower\": 0, \"tasks\": [], \"upper\": 58}, \"random\": {\"attainable\": true, \"exact\": false, \"lower\": 0, \"tasks\": [15], \"upper\": 1}}, \"fraction\": 1.0, \"reference\": {\"attainable\": true, \"exact\": true, \"lower\": 1, \"tasks\": [55], \"upper\": 1}, \"rule\": \"mean\", \"target\": 40, \"validated\": true}\ngrounding keys ['claims']\n0 Task investment selects coordinates updated to round10(x+rho(1-x)); positive caps are 1 and 1/2, co-first tolerance is 1e-10, input rounding is 10 decimals. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n1 The rules are arithmetic mean, ordinary median including averaged central values when even, and pairwise Borda with half-credit ties and updated rivals. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n2 HELM MMLU v1.13.0 contributes 57 subject scores and Open LLM contributes six normalized columns, divided by 100, from pinned revision 9c09a7cae43334062a82cb164f2ef255013dafa2; frozen resources record acquisition on 2026-11-07. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n3 There are eight fixed mean-nonwinner rank-spaced targets per score table; three seeds 42011,42013,42017 repeat the same instances; 48 decisions per family, 96 distinct original instances, 288 original records. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n4 Within any fixed rule and target, increasing rho weakly decreases the minimum budget, including infinity; this does not order different rules. Full-headroom all-task reachability follows structurally from the intervention model. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n101 HELM row 10 reverses mean/median ordering from 9/12 at full cap to 23/12 at half cap. Open LLM row 1609 reverses from 2/3 to 4/3. These are instance counterexamples, not population rates. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n102 All eight original targets per family are reachable under all rules at full cap. At half cap HELM reachability is 5/5/4 and Open LLM is 7/6/3 for mean/median/Borda. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n103 Every original reference interval closes, all finite selected cardinalities match reference minima, and selected subsets repeat identically across three seeds. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n104 Matched greedy equals the finite minimum for original mean and Borda decisions. HELM row28 median at half cap has optimum21 versus greedy52. No component attribution follows. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n105 Permutation, constant and zero-update controls each have 48 validated decisions per family and seed with no case failure; one first-seed replay is recorded as successful and the remaining replay payloads are absent. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n106 Mean sorted gains, odd-median threshold counting, even-median endpoint counting and rival-aware Borda integer gap constraints describe the inspectable supplied selected source; its tree-digest scope is not equated to the final manifest. Borda search has 20000-node limit, 0.9 work allowance and verified incumbent fallback. Exhaustive scalar verification is used when d<=6. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n107 Independent references use exhaustive six-task subsets, exact scalar HELM checks, and time-limited SciPy binary Borda optimization; random and greedy are matched score-space selection policies, not training algorithms. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n108 Development selection had three scored configurations, zero unscored configurations, and zero aggregate difference from the original baseline; no matched final original-baseline delta is available. SOURCES ['study.attempts.total', 'study.attempts.scored', 'study.attempts.unscored', 'study.search_score', 'study.baseline_score', 'study.search_score_delta', 'study.investigation_outcome', 'study.selection_kind']\n109 The independent frozen final assessment is completed and qualified; this does not establish generalization, novelty or superiority. SOURCES ['final.qualification.status', 'final.qualification.outcome', 'final.qualification.correct']\n110 No ablation supports internal component superiority; training-response calibration, strict-margin sensitivity and composition resampling are unavailable. Task budgets are not observed training cost. SOURCES ['final.evidence.episodes']\n111 Background citation consulted within documented scope: Measuring Massive Multitask Language Understanding SOURCES ['ref.exact.Hendrycks2020MMLU']\n112 Background citation consulted within documented scope: Challenging BIG-Bench Tasks and Whether Chain-of-Thought Can Solve Them SOURCES ['ref.exact.Suzgun2022BBH']\n113 Background citation consulted within documented scope: Holistic Evaluation of Language Models SOURCES ['ref.exact.Liang2022HELM']\n114 Background citation consulted within documented scope: The Benchmark Lottery SOURCES ['ref.exact.Dehghani2021Lottery']\n115 Background citation consulted within documented scope: Evaluating Agents using Social Choice Theory SOURCES ['ref.exact.Lanctot2023SocialChoice']\n116 Background citation consulted within documented scope: The Leaderboard Illusion SOURCES ['ref.exact.Singh2025Illusion']\n117 Background citation consulted within documented scope: Don't Make Your LLM an Evaluation Benchmark Cheater SOURCES ['ref.exact.Zhou2023Cheater']\n118 Background citation consulted within documented scope: Rethinking Benchmark and Contamination for Language Models with Rephrased Samples SOURCES ['ref.exact.Yang2023Rephrased']\n119 Background citation consulted within documented scope: Leaderboard Incentives: Model Rankings under Strategic Post-Training SOURCES ['ref.exact.Chen2026Strategic']\n120 Background citation consulted within documented scope: Show Your Work: Improved Reporting of Experimental Results SOURCES ['ref.exact.Dodge2019Reporting']\n121 Background citation consulted within documented scope: A framework for few-shot language model evaluation SOURCES ['ref.exact.Gao2023Harness']\n122 Background citation consulted within documented scope: Handbook of Computational Social Choice SOURCES ['ref.exact.Brandt2016Handbook']\n123 Background citation consulted within documented scope: Man